COMMENT BLOCKS 101-150 — abstract memory architecture;
COMMENT Host/device/shared/local/constant are ALGOL W arrays.;
COMMENT They implement the software memory model. They are not;
COMMENT GPU VRAM. A hardware backend must copy through the;
COMMENT backend interface (BLOCKS 389-390) into real device memory.;
COMMENT ============================================================;

COMMENT BLOCK 101-150;
COMMENT Component: AwgSpaceCap;
COMMENT Purpose: AwgSpaceCap as defined by the following supplied procedure;
COMMENT Inputs: VALUE parameters and referenced global state;
COMMENT Outputs: function result, RESULT parameters and stated global mutations;
COMMENT Dependencies: AwgHead declarations and referenced Awg helpers;
COMMENT Hardware: none (reference software or explicit unavailable status);
COMMENT SOVEREIGN NODE KEY: AWG-PROC-AwgSpaceCap;
COMMENT Parent-ID: AWG-FILE-101AwgMemory;
COMMENT License-ID: SL-AGPL3-001 / MGPLv3;
COMMENT Covenant-Version: 1.0;
COMMENT Copyright: 2026 SNAPKITTYWEST;
COMMENT License-Location: LICENSE;
COMMENT Provenance: docs/NODE_MANIFEST.json;
INTEGER PROCEDURE AwgSpaceCap(INTEGER VALUE Space);
BEGIN
    IF Space = MemHost THEN AwgSpaceCap := CapHost
    ELSE IF Space = MemDevice THEN AwgSpaceCap := CapDev
    ELSE IF Space = MemShared THEN AwgSpaceCap := CapShared
    ELSE IF Space = MemLocal THEN AwgSpaceCap := CapLocal
    ELSE IF Space = MemConstant THEN AwgSpaceCap := CapConst
    ELSE IF Space = MemRegister THEN AwgSpaceCap := CapFreg
    ELSE AwgSpaceCap := 0
END;

